  "content": "<p>Moderate magnitude 4.5 earthquake at 34 km depth</p>\n    <p><i>28 Oct 06:26 UTC</i>: <b>First to report: RaspberryShake after 7 minutes.</b><br /><i>28 Oct 06:28</i>: Now using data updates from CWB</p>\n    \n\n\n    \n    \n        \n            <p>I didn't feel it</p>\n            <p>I felt this quake</p>\n        \n        <h2>Earthquake details</h2>\n        <table>\n\n            <tbody><tr><td>Date &amp; time</td><td>Oct 28, 2026 06:19:00 UTC<b> - </b></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Local time at epicenter</td><td>Wednesday, <b>Oct 28, 2026, at 02:19 pm</b> (Asia/Taipei GMT +8)</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Status</td><td>automatic (likely earthquake, but data not revised by seismologist)</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Magnitude</td><td><b>4.5</b></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Depth</td><td>33.5 km</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Epicenter latitude / longitude</td><td><a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/latlng/23.9/122.4/100/3d.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">23.85°N / 122.44°E</a>  <b><a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/japan.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Japan</a></b><p>Also near:  <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/taiwan.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Taiwan</a> 84 km (52 mi) away</p></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Seismic antipode</td><td><a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/latlng/-23.9/-57.6/500/3d.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">23.85°S / 57.56°W</a> <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/paraguay.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Paraguay</a></td></tr>\n            \n            <tr><td>Shaking intensity</td><td><b>IV</b> Light shaking near epicenter</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Felt</td><td>0 reports</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Primary data source</td><td><a href=\"https://www.cwb.gov.tw/V8/E/E/EQ/EQ115000-1028-141923.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">CWB</a> (Central Weather Bureau)</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Nearest volcano</td><td><a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/unnamed-24-00-n-121-83-e.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Unnamed 24.00°N/121.83°E</a> (64 km / 40 mi)</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Weather at epicenter at time of quake</td><td>Broken Clouds <img src=\"https://openweathermap.org/img/w/04d.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"50\" height=\"50\" /> <b>24.7°C</b> (76 F), humidity: 68%, wind: 9 m/s (18 kts) from NE</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Estimated seismic energy released</td><td>3.5 x 10<sup>11</sup> joules (98.6 megawatt hours, equivalent to 84.8 tons of TNT) | equivalent to <b>ONE quake</b> of magnitude 4.5 | <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/energy.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">about seismic energy</a></td></tr>\n        </tbody></table>\n    \n\n    \n            \n            \n            <p>[smaller] [bigger]</p>\n\n        \n    \n    \n    \n\n    <h2>Nearby places</h2>\n\nThe closest larger town where the quake might have been felt is <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/place/4744/earthquakes/hualien-city.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Hualien City</a>, a town with 99,000 inhabitants in <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/taiwan.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Taiwan</a>, in 86 km (54 mi) distance west of the epicenter. People likely experienced weak shaking there.  In the capital of  <a href=\"https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/taiwan.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Taiwan</a>, Taipei, 163 km (101 mi) away from the epicenter, the earthquake was probably felt as very weak shaking.<br />The following table shows some of the places that might have been affected (or not) by the shaking.<br />\n\n\n\n\n    <table>\n        <thead>\n        <tr>